cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "rctd-split: RCTD + SPLIT typing pipeline (Stage D) with mtx + h5ad export"
message: "If you use this software, please cite it using the metadata from this file."
type: software
authors:
  - name: "xenium-preprocess-pipeline contributors"
version: 0.1.0
date-released: "2026-07-09"
# doi: "10.5281/zenodo.PLACEHOLDER"                    # TODO after Zenodo mint
url: "https://example.org/rctd-split"
repository-code: "https://example.org/rctd-split"
license: MIT
keywords:
  - xenium
  - spatial-transcriptomics
  - RCTD
  - SPLIT
  - celltype-annotation
  - spacexr
abstract: >-
  rctd-split is step 4 of the Xenium spatial-data preprocessing
  pipeline. It runs RCTD (via spacexr) against a spatial test object
  (Stage A/step 1 output) and a scRNA reference (Stage C/step 3
  output), then applies SPLIT::run_post_process_RCTD (unpurified) and
  SPLIT::purify (purified). Deliverables per sample: the RCTD results
  RDS, unpurified and purified Seurat RDS, matched 10x-style mtx bundles
  (counts + features + barcodes + metadata + spatial coordinates), and
  the same two variants materialised as .h5ad AnnData files ready for
  downstream Python analysis. Adapted from an internal SPLIT/Proseg
  workflow.
